        <instructions><![CDATA[<p><strong>Mental health</strong></p>
<div>
<p>Coaching, support, referral to resources, and overall health evaluation (initial and follow-up meetings). </p>
</div>
<div>
<p>* Nurse counsellors cannot give prescriptions or medical notes.</p>
</div>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>Medical, physical health</strong></p>
<div>
<p>Coaching, support, referral to resources, and overall health evaluation. </p>
</div>
<div>
<p>* Nurse counsellors cannot give prescriptions or medical notes. </p>
<p> </p>
<div>
<p><strong>Work-related illness or injury </strong></p>
</div>
<div>
<p>During the consultation with an employee who has a work-related illness or injury, the nurse counsellor will conduct an assessment, refer the employee to a health care professional and guide them through the next steps, working with the Disability Management team or following the Workplace Safety and Insurance Board (WSIB) process as required. </p>
</div>
</div>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>Health resources</strong></p>
<div>
<p>Referral to community resources, such as professional health care providers (e.g. walk-in clinics, optometrists, physiotherapists, support groups). </p>
</div>
<div>
<p>* No referrals to medical specialists. </p>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>Respiratory illnesses (cold, flu, COVID, etc.)</strong></p>
<div>
<p>Nurse counsellors can answer questions or concerns related to respiratory illnesses or COVID. </p>
</div>
<div>
<p>You can also visit <a href="https://hoccdc.sharepoint.com/sites/atrium/en/Pages/service.aspx?s&#61;/sites/info/en/services/health-wellness/Pages/COVID-19-SITUATION-UPDATE-FOR-HOC-EMPLOYEES.aspx&amp;u&#61;/sites/info/en/services/health-wellness/&amp;n&#61;COVID-19-SITUATION-UPDATE-FOR-HOC-EMPLOYEES&amp;cg&#61;%28acg:%22071c070c-abf7-4d9a-9601-9b425668fc61%22%29&amp;pr&#61;%22empty%22&amp;sb&#61;%28sbj:%22b2ce43b9-2d92-4180-bf78-3f8fff86cb73%22%29" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Atrium</a> for information on this topic. </p>
<p> </p>
<div>
<p><strong>Advisory/</strong><strong>coaching service</strong>s </p>
</div>
<div>
<p>Advice and coaching on wellness to support an employee or teams in maintaining and improving their overall health and well-being. These services may include one-on-one consultations, health education and practical guidance tailored to individual needs. </p>
</div>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>Training/education</strong></p>
<p>The health and wellness team can assess your team’s needs and recommend appropriate training solutions or offer on-demand training opportunities related to mental and physical health. </p>
</div>
</div>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>On-site crisis support</strong></p>
<p>Following a stressful or traumatic event related to the workplace, such as the loss of a colleague or an incident in the workplace, the health and wellness team can arrange on-site support through the Employee and Family Assistance Program (EFAP). A qualified mental health professional (e.g. a psychotherapist) can be sent to provide individual or group interventions to help employees process and cope with the situation. </p>
<p> </p>
<div>
<p><strong>Psychological health and safety </strong></p>
</div>
<div>
<p>The health and wellness team provides proactive, preventative and responsive services designed to enhance mental well-being, minimize psychological risk factors and foster a supportive workplace culture. </p>
</div>
<div>
<p> </p>
</div>
<div>
<p><strong>Other (please specify below)</strong> </p>
</div>
<div>
<p>Any other services not listed above. </p>
</div>
<div> </div>]]></instructions>
